---
pagination:
  data: projectPages
  size: 1
  alias: project
permalink: "/projects/{{ project.slug }}/"
layout: layouts/base.njk
eleventyComputed:
  title: "{{ project.name | safe }}"
  description: "{{ project.tagline | safe }} What it owns in the Knowledge Islands ecosystem, and where its canonical source lives."
---
{% from "macros/icons.njk" import kiIcon %}

{#
  One template for every project, including the four that ship a binary.
  `version` is the marker: a released tool carries it along with `maturity`,
  `formula`, `installer`, `manual` and `changelog`, and everything below that
  reads those fields is guarded by it. A tool page therefore gains the install
  material without a separate section or a second template (KI-WEB-SITE-020).
#}
{%- set released = project.version is defined %}

<section class="section-navy hero-section hero-section-standard">
  <div class="page-container" style="max-width: 64rem;">
    <p class="overline-gold">Projects / <code>{{ project.name }}</code></p>
    <h1 class="heading-display-light" style="font-size: clamp(2.25rem, 4vw, 3.25rem); margin-bottom: 1.25rem; max-width: 22ch;">{{ project.tagline }}</h1>
    <p style="font-size: 1.125rem; color: rgb(245 239 224 / 75%); max-width: 54ch; line-height: 1.7;">{{ project.description }}</p>
    {%- if released %}
    <p style="margin-top: 1.5rem; font-size: 0.9375rem; color: rgb(245 239 224 / 60%);">Released command-line tool · currently published as <code>{{ project.version }}</code> · {{ project.maturity }}</p>
    {%- else %}
    <p style="margin-top: 1.5rem; font-size: 0.9375rem; color: rgb(245 239 224 / 60%);">Public {{ project.kind }} repository · {{ project.availability }}</p>
    {%- endif %}
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section-parchment section-pad">
  <div class="page-container" style="max-width: 64rem;">
    <div class="grid-2col" style="gap: 3rem; align-items: start;">
      <div class="prose-ki" style="max-width: none;">
        <p class="overline">Authority</p>
        <h2>What this repository owns.</h2>
        <p>{{ project.role }}</p>
        <p>That boundary is deliberate. The ecosystem separates philosophy, engineering discipline, capability semantics, portable standards, and executable behaviour so that none of them can quietly absorb another. <a href="/projects/">The full directory</a> shows where this project sits relative to the rest.</p>

        <p class="overline" style="margin-top: 2.5rem;">Using it</p>
        <h2>How to pick it up today.</h2>
        <p>{{ project.usage }}</p>
      </div>

      <aside class="card-ki">
        <div class="symbol-circle symbol-circle-{{ project.accent }}">{{ kiIcon(project.icon, 22) }}</div>
        <h2 style="font-size: 1.125rem; margin-bottom: 0.75rem;"><code>{{ project.name }}</code> at source.</h2>
        <p class="text-muted" style="font-size: 0.9375rem;">The repository is the authority for this project's contents, its interfaces and its current state. This page describes it; it does not stand in for it.</p>
        {%- if released %}
        <p style="margin: 0.75rem 0 0;"><a href="{{ project.manual }}">Read the manual</a></p>
        <p style="margin: 0.375rem 0 0;"><a href="{{ project.changelog }}">Release history</a></p>
        <p style="margin: 0.375rem 0 0;"><a href="{{ project.repository }}">Open the repository</a></p>
        {%- else %}
        <p style="margin: 0.75rem 0 0;"><a href="{{ project.repository }}">Open the repository</a></p>
        <p style="margin: 0.375rem 0 0;"><a href="{{ project.repository }}#readme">Read the README</a></p>
        {%- endif %}
      </aside>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{%- if released %}
<section class="section-mist section-pad">
  <div class="page-container" style="max-width: 64rem;">
    <div class="prose-ki" style="max-width: none;">
      <p class="overline">Install</p>
      {% if project.formula %}
      <h2>Prefer Homebrew.</h2>
      <p>The <a href="https://github.com/knowledgeislands/homebrew-tap">Knowledge Islands tap</a> packages <code>{{ project.name }}</code>, so Homebrew owns upgrades and removal. Naming the tap in the argument taps it implicitly.</p>
      <pre style="overflow-x: auto; padding: 1rem; border-radius: var(--radius-md); background: var(--color-navy); color: var(--color-parchment); font-size: 0.8125rem;"><code>brew install knowledgeislands/tap/{{ project.formula }}</code></pre>
      <h2>Or use the stable installer endpoint.</h2>
      {% else %}
      <h2>Use the stable installer endpoint.</h2>
      {% endif %}
      <p>The URL below is this site's stable machine route. It redirects to the installer published at <code>{{ project.version }}</code> in <a href="{{ project.repository }}">the source repository</a>, which owns the installer's behaviour and any signature or checksum verification it performs.</p>
      <pre style="overflow-x: auto; padding: 1rem; border-radius: var(--radius-md); background: var(--color-navy); color: var(--color-parchment); font-size: 0.8125rem;"><code>curl -fsSL {{ site.url }}/install/{{ project.slug }} | sh</code></pre>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
{%- endif %}

<section class="{{ "section-parchment" if released else "section-mist" }} section-pad">
  <div class="page-container" style="max-width: 64rem;">
    <div class="prose-ki" style="max-width: none;">
      <p class="overline">Nearby</p>
      <h2>{{ "The rest of the released set." if released else "Other projects of the same kind." }}</h2>
      <ul>
        {%- for other in projects %}
          {%- if other.kind == project.kind and other.slug != project.slug %}
        <li><a href="{{ other.route | default('/projects/' + other.slug + '/') }}"><code>{{ other.name }}</code></a> — {{ other.tagline }}</li>
          {%- endif %}
        {%- endfor %}
      </ul>
      <p>See <a href="/projects/">every public project</a>, or go straight to <a href="/projects/#tool">the released command-line tools</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
